   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## Stage 1 – Image Preprocessing\n\nThe preprocessing pipeline converts a raw document scan into a clean, binarized, deskewed image ready for layout analysis. Steps:\n1. Load and resize the image\n2. Convert to greyscale\n3. Noise reduction (Gaussian / Bilateral / Morphological)\n4. Binarization (Otsu / Adaptive Gaussian / Sauvola)\n5. Geometric correction (Hough-based deskew + perspective correction)"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "97195c85",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "### 1.0 Synthetic Document Generator\n\nSince no physical scans are provided we synthesise a realistic document image that exhibits the degradations the pipeline must handle: Gaussian noise, skew, uneven illumination and mixed content (header, body text, table)."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a4b6299e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "def make_synthetic_document(skew_deg=4.0, noise_sigma=15, width=700, height=900):\n    \"\"\"Create a white A4-like document with text, a table and noise/skew.\"\"\"\n    img = np.ones((height, width), dtype=np.uint8) * 255\n\n    font      = cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX\n    font_bold = cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_DUPLEX\n\n    # Header\n    cv2.putText(img, \"INVOICE #2024-0042\", (40, 60),  font_bold, 1.0,  0, 2)\n    cv2.putText(img, \"University of Ruhuna – Accounts Dept.\", (40, 100), font, 0.6, 0, 1)\n    cv2.line(img, (40, 115), (660, 115), 0, 2)\n\n    # Body text\n    body = [\n        \"Bill To: Department of EIE\",\n        \"Date: 23 January 2026\",\n        \"Due Date: 07 February 2026\",\n        \"Payment Method: Bank Transfer\",\n        \"\",\n        \"Description of Services Rendered:\",\n        \"  - Image Processing Lab Equipment\",\n        \"  - Computer Vision Licence Fees\",\n        \"  - Software Maintenance Contract\",\n    ]\n    y = 145\n    for line in body:\n        cv2.putText(img, line, (40, y), font, 0.52, 0, 1)\n        y += 28\n\n    # Table\n    cols = [40, 280, 430, 560, 660]\n    rows_y = list(range(360, 560, 40))\n    for ry in rows_y:\n        cv2.line(img, (cols[0], ry), (cols[-1], ry), 0, 1)\n    for cx in cols:\n        cv2.line(img, (cx, rows_y[0]), (cx, rows_y[-1]), 0, 1)\n\n    headers = [\"Item\", \"Description\", \"Qty\", \"Unit Price\", \"Total\"]\n    data_rows = [\n        [\"001\", \"HOG Descriptor Kit\",  \"2\",  \"LKR 12500\", \"LKR 25000\"],\n        [\"002\", \"SVM Licence\",          \"1\",  \"LKR 45000\", \"LKR 45000\"],\n        [\"003\", \"k-NN Module\",          \"3\",  \"LKR 8000\",  \"LKR 24000\"],\n        [\"004\", \"Tesseract OCR\",        \"1\",  \"LKR 0\",     \"LKR 0\"   ],\n    ]\n    for ci, h in enumerate(headers):\n        cv2.putText(img, h, (cols[ci] + 5, rows_y[0] + 25), font, 0.45, 0, 1)\n    for ri, row in enumerate(data_rows):\n        for ci, cell in enumerate(row):\n            cv2.putText(img, cell, (cols[ci] + 5, rows_y[ri + 1] + 25), font, 0.42, 0, 1)\n\n    # Footer\n    cv2.line(img, (40, 830), (660, 830), 0, 1)\n    cv2.putText(img, \"Total Due: LKR 94,000.00\", (400, 860), font_bold, 0.65, 0, 2)\n    cv2.putText(img, \"Thank you for your business!\", (40, 880), font, 0.45, 100, 1)\n\n    # Add Gaussian noise\n    noise = np.random.normal(0, noise_sigma, img.shape).astype(np.int16)\n    img = np.clip(img.astype(np.int16) + noise, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n\n    # Apply skew\n    h, w = img.shape\n    center = (w // 2, h // 2)\n    M = cv2.getRotationMatrix2D(center, skew_deg, 1.0)\n    skewed = cv2.warpAffine(img, M, (w, h),\n                             flags=cv2.INTER_LINEAR,\n                             borderValue=255)\n    return skewed\n\n\n# Generate and display\ndoc_image = make_synthetic_document(skew_deg=4.0, noise_sigma=18)\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 10))\nplt.imshow(doc_image, cmap='gray')\nplt.title('Synthetic Document (with noise + 4° skew)', fontsize=13)\nplt.axis('off')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\nprint(f\"Image shape: {doc_image.shape}  |  dtype: {doc_image.dtype}\")"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "57357417",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "### 1.1 Noise Reduction\n\nThree filters are compared:\n- **Gaussian Blur** – fast, isotropic smoothing; blurs edges\n- **Bilateral Filter** – edge-preserving smoothing; slower but superior for text\n- **Median Blur** – removes salt-and-pepper noise; non-linear"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d883f5c0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "nr = NoiseReducer()\n\ngaussian  = nr.gaussian_blur(doc_image, kernel_size=5, sigma=1.0)\nbilateral = nr.bilateral_filter(doc_image, diameter=9, sigma_color=75, sigma_space=75)\nmedian    = nr.median_blur(doc_image, kernel_size=3)\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 4, figsize=(18, 5))\ntitles = ['Original (noisy)', 'Gaussian Blur', 'Bilateral Filter', 'Median Blur']\nimages = [doc_image, gaussian, bilateral, median]\nfor ax, img, title in zip(axes, images, titles):\n    ax.imshow(img, cmap='gray', vmin=0, vmax=255)\n    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=11)\n    ax.axis('off')\nplt.suptitle('1.1 Noise Reduction Comparison', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\n# Quantify noise reduction using standard deviation (lower = smoother)\nfor name, img in zip(titles, images):\n    print(f\"  {name:20s}  std = {img.std():.2f}\")"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7e6ff5d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "### 1.2 Binarization\n\nConverting the greyscale image to a binary (black/white) image isolates text pixels from the background.\n\n| Method | Mechanism | Best for |\n|--------|-----------|----------|\n| **Otsu** | Global threshold minimising intra-class variance | Uniform lighting |\n| **Adaptive Gaussian** | Local threshold per neighbourhood | Uneven illumination |\n| **Sauvola** | Local mean + std, tuned for documents | Aged/degraded scans |"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1b0b20c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "binarizer = Binarizer()\ndenoised  = bilateral  # use bilateral-filtered image for binarization\n\notsu_bin,  otsu_thresh = binarizer.otsu_threshold(denoised)\nadap_bin               = binarizer.adaptive_threshold(denoised, block_size=25, C=8)\nsauv_bin               = binarizer.sauvola_threshold(denoised, window_size=25, k=0.2)\n\n# Morphological clean-up on Otsu result\notsu_clean = binarizer.apply_morphology(otsu_bin, operation='open', kernel_size=2)\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 4, figsize=(18, 5))\ntitles = [f'Otsu (T={otsu_thresh:.0f})', 'Otsu + Morph Open',\n          'Adaptive Gaussian', 'Sauvola']\nimgs   = [otsu_bin, otsu_clean, adap_bin, sauv_bin]\nfor ax, img, title in zip(axes, imgs, titles):\n    ax.imshow(img, cmap='gray')\n    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=11)\n    ax.axis('off')\nplt.suptitle('1.2 Binarization Methods', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\nbinary_image = otsu_clean  # forward to next stages\nprint(f\"Otsu global threshold: {otsu_thresh:.1f}  |  \"\n      f\"Black pixel ratio: {(binary_image == 0).mean():.3f}\")"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fcee5bd9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "### 1.3 Geometric Correction\n\n**Deskewing** uses the Hough Transform to estimate the dominant line angle in the document and counter-rotates.  \n**Perspective correction** uses Harris corner detection to locate the four document corners and applies a homographic warp."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "40654ee1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "corrector = GeometricCorrector()\n\n# Skew detection and correction\ndetected_angle = corrector.detect_skew_angle(binary_image)\ndeskewed_bin   = corrector.deskew_image(binary_image, detected_angle)\ndeskewed_gray  = corrector.deskew_image(denoised, detected_angle)\n\nprint(f\"Detected skew angle: {detected_angle:.2f}°  (injected: 4.0°)\")\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(16, 6))\naxes[0].imshow(doc_image, cmap='gray');  axes[0].set_title('Original (4° skew)');  axes[0].axis('off')\naxes[1].imshow(binary_image, cmap='gray'); axes[1].set_title('Binarized (skewed)'); axes[1].axis('off')\naxes[2].imshow(deskewed_bin, cmap='gray'); axes[2].set_title(f'Deskewed ({detected_angle:.1f}° corrected)'); axes[2].axis('off')\nplt.suptitle('1.3 Geometric Correction – Deskewing', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\n# Harris corner detection demo\ncorners = corrector.detect_corners(deskewed_gray)\ncorner_img = cv2.cvtColor(deskewed_gray, cv2.COLOR_GRAY2BGR)\nfor pt in corners:\n    cv2.circle(corner_img, (int(pt[0]), int(pt[1])), 10, (0, 0, 255), 3)\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(6, 8))\nplt.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(corner_img, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\nplt.title('Harris Corner Detection (document corners in red)')\nplt.axis('off')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\nbinary_image = deskewed_bin   # forward clean binary"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "98d397d1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## Stage 2 – Document Layout Analysis\n\nLayout analysis locates and classifies the regions of a document (text blocks, tables, images, headers/footers) before feeding individual character patches to the recogniser.\n\nPipeline:\n1. **Connected Component Analysis** – label every foreground blob\n2. **Contour Detection** – find structural boundaries\n3. **RLSA** – merge nearby characters into text blocks\n4. **X-Y Cut** – recursive whitespace-based segmentation\n5. **Region Classification** – label each segment by content type"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9b520da4",
   "source": "### 2.1 Connected Component Analysis\n\nEach isolated foreground blob is labelled. Features extracted: bounding box, pixel area, density, centroid, and aspect ratio.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "b886a6a6",
   "source": "cc_analyzer = ConnectedComponentAnalyzer()\n\ninv_binary = cv2.bitwise_not(binary_image)  # CC wants foreground = 255\ncomponents, labels_map = cc_analyzer.find_components(inv_binary)\nfiltered_comps = cc_analyzer.filter_components(\n    components, min_area=30, max_area=5000, min_aspect=0.1, max_aspect=15\n)\n\nvis = cc_analyzer.draw_components(\n    cv2.cvtColor(binary_image, cv2.COLOR_GRAY2BGR), filtered_comps\n)\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(18, 7))\naxes[0].imshow(binary_image, cmap='gray');           axes[0].set_title('Binarized Image');         axes[0].axis('off')\naxes[1].imshow(labels_map, cmap='nipy_spectral');    axes[1].set_title('Connected Component Labels'); axes[1].axis('off')\naxes[2].imshow(cv2.cvtColor(vis, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)); axes[2].set_title(f'Filtered Components (n={len(filtered_comps)})'); axes[2].axis('off')\nplt.suptitle('2.1 Connected Component Analysis', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n\n# Summary statistics\nareas = [c['area'] for c in filtered_comps]\nprint(f\"Total components (raw): {len(components)}\")\nprint(f\"Filtered components:    {len(filtered_comps)}\")\nprint(f\"Area  – min: {min(areas):.0f}  max: {max(areas):.0f}  mean: {np.mean(areas):.1f}\")",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "265d2254",
   "source": "### 2.2 Contour Detection\n\n`cv2.findContours` returns closed curves around foreground regions. Filtering by area and aspect ratio keeps character-sized contours.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "924aa67f",
   "source": "cd = ContourDetector()\nall_regions   = cd.detect_contours(inv_binary)\ntext_regions  = cd.filter_text_contours(all_regions, min_area=80)\n\nvis_contours = cd.draw_contours(\n    cv2.cvtColor(binary_image, cv2.COLOR_GRAY2BGR), text_regions, color=(0, 0, 200)\n)\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 7))\naxes[0].imshow(binary_image, cmap='gray');                           axes[0].set_title('Binary Input');   axes[0].axis('off')\naxes[1].imshow(cv2.cvtColor(vis_contours, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB));       axes[1].set_title(f'Text Contours (n={len(text_regions)})'); axes[1].axis('off')\nplt.suptitle('2.2 Contour Detection', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\nprint(f\"All contours: {len(all_regions)}  |  After filtering: {len(text_regions)}\")",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "deb8a5c1",
   "source": "### 2.3 Run-Length Smoothing Algorithm (RLSA)\n\nRLSA bridges small horizontal gaps between characters to group them into words, and small vertical gaps to group words into text blocks.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "72a6f4dd",
   "source": "rlsa = RLSAProcessor()\n\nh_smooth   = rlsa.horizontal_rlsa(binary_image, threshold=40)\nv_smooth   = rlsa.vertical_rlsa(binary_image,   threshold=15)\ncombined   = rlsa.combined_rlsa(binary_image,   h_thresh=40, v_thresh=15)\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 4, figsize=(20, 6))\nfor ax, img, title in zip(axes,\n        [binary_image, h_smooth, v_smooth, combined],\n        ['Binary', 'Horizontal RLSA', 'Vertical RLSA', 'Combined RLSA']):\n    ax.imshow(img, cmap='gray')\n    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=11)\n    ax.axis('off')\nplt.suptitle('2.3 Run-Length Smoothing Algorithm', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "de833263",
   "source": "### 2.4 X-Y Cut Segmentation\n\nThe X-Y Cut algorithm recursively splits the page on whitespace: first it looks for a large horizontal gap (cut in Y), then a vertical one (cut in X), until regions are small enough to leave as leaf segments.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "5dc7fcb3",
   "source": "xy_cutter = XYCutSegmenter(min_region_width=60, min_region_height=20, gap_threshold=6)\nxy_regions = xy_cutter.segment(combined)   # operate on RLSA-smoothed image\n\nvis_xy = cv2.cvtColor(binary_image, cv2.COLOR_GRAY2BGR)\ncolors = plt.cm.Set1(np.linspace(0, 1, min(len(xy_regions), 9)))\nfor i, (x, y, w, h) in enumerate(xy_regions):\n    c = tuple(int(v * 255) for v in colors[i % 9][:3])\n    cv2.rectangle(vis_xy, (x, y), (x + w, y + h), c[::-1], 2)\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 10))\nplt.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(vis_xy, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\nplt.title(f'2.4 X-Y Cut Segmentation  ({len(xy_regions)} regions)', fontsize=13)\nplt.axis('off'); plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\nprint(f\"Segments found: {len(xy_regions)}\")",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5ee7ca4c",
   "source": "### 2.5 Region Classification\n\nEach segment is classified based on its position (header / footer zones), horizontal line density (table detection), and foreground pixel density (image vs text).",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "8b7b9fd2",
   "source": "classifier = RegionClassifier()\nclassified_regions = classifier.classify_all(binary_image, xy_regions)\n\ntype_colors = {\n    'header_footer': (255, 100, 0),\n    'table':         (0, 180, 255),\n    'text':          (0, 200, 0),\n    'image':         (180, 0, 255),\n    'unknown':       (120, 120, 120),\n}\n\nvis_class = cv2.cvtColor(binary_image, cv2.COLOR_GRAY2BGR)\nfor r in classified_regions:\n    x, y, w, h = r['bbox']\n    color = type_colors.get(r['type'], (128, 128, 128))\n    cv2.rectangle(vis_class, (x, y), (x + w, y + h), color[::-1], 2)\n    cv2.putText(vis_class, r['type'][:3], (x + 2, y + 14),\n                cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.35, color[::-1], 1)\n\n# Legend\nlegend_patches = [mpatches.Patch(color=np.array(c)/255, label=t)\n                  for t, c in type_colors.items()]\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 10))\nax.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(vis_class, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\nax.set_title('2.5 Region Classification', fontsize=13)\nax.axis('off')\nax.legend(handles=legend_patches, loc='lower right', fontsize=9)\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n\nfrom collections import Counter\ncounts = Counter(r['type'] for r in classified_regions)\nprint(\"Region type counts:\", dict(counts))",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8e7a2a87",
   "source": "## Stage 3 – Character Recognition\n\nThe recognition pipeline:\n1. Extract character patches from connected components\n2. Normalise each patch to 32×32 pixels\n3. Compute HOG (Histogram of Oriented Gradients) feature vector\n4. Classify with SVM (RBF kernel) and k-NN\n5. Fall back to template matching when classifier confidence is low\n6. Assemble characters into words based on horizontal spacing",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "77629fb6",
   "source": "### 3.1 Character Patch Extraction and Normalisation",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "6492a58f",
   "source": "norm = CharacterNormalizer()\n\n# Extract patches for the first 30 filtered components\nsample_comps  = filtered_comps[:30]\npatches = norm.extract_char_patches(binary_image, sample_comps, padding=2)\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 10, figsize=(16, 5))\nfor i, (ax, patch) in enumerate(zip(axes.flat, patches)):\n    ax.imshow(patch, cmap='gray')\n    x, y, w, h = sample_comps[i]['bbox']\n    ax.set_title(f'{w}×{h}', fontsize=6)\n    ax.axis('off')\nplt.suptitle('3.1 Normalised 32×32 Character Patches (first 30)', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\nprint(f\"Patch shape: {patches[0].shape}\")",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c610273f",
   "source": "### 3.2 HOG Feature Extraction\n\nHOG counts gradient orientations in local cells. For a 32×32 patch with 4×4 cells and 9 orientation bins the descriptor is 324 dimensions.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "4871ae51",
   "source": "hog_extractor = HOGFeatureExtractor()\n\n# Show descriptor for one patch\nsample_patch = patches[0]\ndescriptor = hog_extractor.extract(sample_patch)\n\nprint(f\"HOG descriptor length: {len(descriptor)}\")\nprint(f\"Descriptor stats  – min: {descriptor.min():.4f}  max: {descriptor.max():.4f}  mean: {descriptor.mean():.4f}\")\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\naxes[0].imshow(sample_patch, cmap='gray')\naxes[0].set_title('Input patch (32×32)')\naxes[0].axis('off')\naxes[1].bar(range(len(descriptor)), descriptor, color='steelblue', width=1.0)\naxes[1].set_title(f'HOG Descriptor ({len(descriptor)} dims)')\naxes[1].set_xlabel('Dimension')\naxes[1].set_ylabel('Magnitude')\nplt.suptitle('3.2 HOG Feature Extraction', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n\n# Extract features for all patches\nall_features = hog_extractor.extract_batch(patches)\nprint(f\"Feature matrix shape: {all_features.shape}\")",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ddd5d336",
   "source": "### 3.3 SVM and k-NN Training (sklearn digits dataset)\n\nWe train on `sklearn.datasets.load_digits` (8×8 MNIST-like digit images, 1797 samples, 10 classes) to demonstrate the full classifier pipeline.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "02bc49d0",
   "source": "from sklearn.datasets import load_digits\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n\ndigits = load_digits()\n\n# Resize each 8x8 patch to 32x32 and extract HOG\nhog_ext  = HOGFeatureExtractor()\nscaler   = StandardScaler()\n\ndef prepare_digits(data):\n    imgs = (data * 16).astype(np.uint8)          # scale to [0,255]\n    imgs_32 = np.array([cv2.resize(img, (32, 32)) for img in imgs])\n    feats = hog_ext.extract_batch(imgs_32)\n    return feats\n\nX = prepare_digits(digits.images)\ny = [str(d) for d in digits.target]\n\nX_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X)\nX_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n    X_scaled, y, test_size=0.2, random_state=42, stratify=y\n)\n\nprint(f\"Dataset: {len(X)} samples, {X.shape[1]} HOG features, {len(set(y))} classes\")\nprint(f\"Train: {len(X_train)}  |  Test: {len(X_test)}\")\n\n# Show sample digits\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 10, figsize=(14, 3))\nfor i, ax in enumerate(axes.flat):\n    ax.imshow(digits.images[i], cmap='gray_r')\n    ax.set_title(str(digits.target[i]), fontsize=9)\n    ax.axis('off')\nplt.suptitle('3.3 Sample digits (sklearn dataset)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "0c2e0954",
   "source": "# Train SVM\nt0 = time.time()\nsvm_clf = SVMClassifier(kernel='rbf', C=10.0, gamma='scale')\nsvm_clf.train(X_train, y_train)\nsvm_time = time.time() - t0\n\nsvm_preds = svm_clf.predict(X_test)\nsvm_acc   = np.mean(np.array(svm_preds) == np.array(y_test))\n\n# Train k-NN\nt0 = time.time()\nknn_clf = KNNClassifier(n_neighbors=5)\nknn_clf.train(X_train, y_train)\nknn_time = time.time() - t0\n\nknn_preds = knn_clf.predict(X_test)\nknn_acc   = np.mean(np.array(knn_preds) == np.array(y_test))\n\nprint(f\"SVM  – accuracy: {svm_acc*100:.2f}%  |  train time: {svm_time:.2f}s\")\nprint(f\"k-NN – accuracy: {knn_acc*100:.2f}%  |  train time: {knn_time:.2f}s\")\nprint()\nprint(\"=== SVM Classification Report ===\")\nprint(classification_report(y_test, svm_preds))",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "f5d7a512",
   "source": "# Confusion matrices\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 6))\nfor ax, preds, title in zip(axes,\n        [svm_preds, knn_preds],\n        ['SVM (RBF kernel)', 'k-NN (k=5)']):\n    cm = confusion_matrix(y_test, preds, labels=[str(i) for i in range(10)])\n    disp = ConfusionMatrixDisplay(cm, display_labels=[str(i) for i in range(10)])\n    disp.plot(ax=ax, colorbar=False, cmap='Blues')\n    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=12)\nplt.suptitle('3.3 Confusion Matrices – HOG + Classifier', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n\n# Accuracy bar chart\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5, 4))\nax.bar(['SVM', 'k-NN'], [svm_acc*100, knn_acc*100], color=['steelblue', 'coral'])\nax.axhline(90, color='green', linestyle='--', label='Target 90%')\nax.set_ylim(0, 105)\nax.set_ylabel('Accuracy (%)')\nax.set_title('Character Recognition Accuracy')\nax.legend()\nfor i, v in enumerate([svm_acc, knn_acc]):\n    ax.text(i, v*100 + 1, f'{v*100:.1f}%', ha='center', fontweight='bold')\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()",
