  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "653cda44",
   "source": "## Stage 4 – Post-Processing\n\nAfter recognition, raw text is refined by:\n1. **Context Verification** – rule-based substitution of known OCR confusions (0↔O, 1↔l, etc.)\n2. **Spell Correction** – Levenshtein-distance matching against a domain dictionary\n3. **Output Formatting** – plain text, JSON, or CSV",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a052f86f",
   "source": "### 4.1 Levenshtein Distance\n\nThe edit distance between two strings counts the minimum number of single-character insertions, deletions, or substitutions to transform one into the other.",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "e6f5d6bd",
   "source": "# Demonstrate Levenshtein distance\npairs = [\n    (\"invoice\", \"lnvoice\"),    # OCR confusion i→l\n    (\"total\",   \"t0tal\"),      # 0 instead of o\n    (\"receipt\", \"recei pt\"),   # extra space\n    (\"january\", \"ianuary\"),    # j/i confusion\n    (\"address\", \"adress\"),     # missing d\n]\nprint(f\"{'String 1':15s}  {'String 2':15s}  {'Edit Distance':>14}\")\nprint(\"-\" * 50)\nfor s1, s2 in pairs:\n    d = levenshtein_distance(s1, s2)\n    print(f\"  {s1:13s}  {s2:13s}  {d:>14}\")\n\n# Visualise distance matrix for a small vocabulary\nvocab = [\"the\", \"that\", \"this\", \"them\", \"then\", \"there\"]\nmatrix = np.array([[levenshtein_distance(a, b) for b in vocab] for a in vocab])\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 5))\nim = ax.imshow(matrix, cmap='YlOrRd_r')\nax.set_xticks(range(len(vocab))); ax.set_xticklabels(vocab, rotation=45)\nax.set_yticks(range(len(vocab))); ax.set_yticklabels(vocab)\nfor i in range(len(vocab)):\n    for j in range(len(vocab)):\n        ax.text(j, i, str(matrix[i, j]), ha='center', va='center', fontsize=11)\nplt.colorbar(im, ax=ax, label='Edit Distance')\nax.set_title('4.1 Levenshtein Distance Matrix')\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
