   "id": "39c4c6f0",
   "source": "## Stage 5 – Full Pipeline Integration and Evaluation\n\nThe `OCRPipeline` class ties together all four stages. Here we:\n1. Save the synthetic document to disk\n2. Run the complete pipeline on it (Tesseract back-end for word recognition)\n3. Compute CER, WER, and IoU against ground-truth\n4. Display a timing breakdown",
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "f40cbf48",
   "source": "import tempfile, os\n\n# Save the clean (no skew) version so Tesseract gives best results\nclean_doc = make_synthetic_document(skew_deg=0.0, noise_sigma=5)\nwith tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(suffix='.png', delete=False) as f:\n    tmp_path = f.name\ncv2.imwrite(tmp_path, clean_doc)\n\npipeline = OCRPipeline(\n    binarization='otsu',\n    correct_skew=True,\n    use_tesseract=True,\n    output_format='json',\n)\n\nresult = pipeline.run(tmp_path)\nos.unlink(tmp_path)\n\nprint(\"=== Pipeline Metrics ===\")\nfor k, v in result['metrics'].items():\n    print(f\"  {k:25s}: {v}\")\nprint()\nprint(\"=== JSON Output (truncated) ===\")\nprint(result['output'][:600])",
